lens:
Luxury art direction for jewellery e-commerce (Mejuri / Missoma / Monica Vinader calibre) with Indian fine-jewellery taste, round 4: elegance, typography, photography sequence and crops, spacing and grid, colour, hierarchy, copy tone, and whether a Rs 2,399 piece feels worth desiring.

G3 passes. fold.png, added.png, fold-ad.png, screens_1-3.jpg and measure.json (04:30:23-27) are newer than prototype.html (04:28:28), and my own renders of the untouched file (md5 49edcb03...) match them. fold-ad.png is byte-identical to fold.png (md5 ab13225d...), by the builder's choice: prism_sugar_p1 carries no confirmed angle. I found no G1 trip from this lens.

All eight of my round-3 fixes landed. Three changes from round 3 made things worse from this lens, and the fixes below undo them:
- my own 'Play plate on both tiles' now covers the bracelet's lower links in tile 1;
- the WhatsApp fit link stacks a second link in the spec table and leaves a 92px hole in it;
- the bag's new foot line means a two-piece bag states the saving three times, 'automatic' each time.

Evidence is in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/r4art:
- probe.js and probe.json: boxes, the text-style census and the colours in use;
- s2x_00..05.jpg: the page as 2x phone screens;
- slide_0..6.png and gallery_r4.jpg: every gallery slide;
- added_1.png, added_ring.png, drawer_1.png, drawer_2.png, set_after.png, viewer.png and land_riya.png;
- fold_320x568.png, fold_412x732.png, fold_390x844.png and folds_3.jpg;
- scr_500.png, scr_1900.png and scr_2380.png: real scroll positions;
- src_r4.jpg: the creator frames, the chip crop and the set sprite.
Fixes 1-5 were injected into the untouched file at runtime, never into the prototype: mock.js produced mock_set.png, mock_specs.png, mock_dl72.png, mock_riya.png, mock_card.png, mock_card_ring.png, mock_drawer2.png and mock_drawer4.png. card.js, dl.js and ov.js measured the card heights, the spec table and the set rows at 320 and 360. bar320.js measured the bar labels.

score_now is the weighted mean of the same criteria as rounds 1-3 (C1, C2, C7, C10, C12, C13, C14, C18, C19, C20): 406.8 / 46 = 8.84, reported as 8.8. The critique is also written to /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/pdp10/rounds/r4_art.json.

criteria.note:
Unchanged, and right. At 360x640 the order is photo, name, price, ladder, delivery (measure.json, probe.json):
- the hero at 77-386;
- the Cormorant 27 H1 at 398-426;
- the price row at 432-461;
- the ruled ladder at 471-538;
- 'Free insured delivery, est. 18–20 Nov · COD available' at 544-562;
- the bar at 575.
Nothing wraps at 320, 360, 390 or 412 (folds_3.jpg).

It holds at 9 rather than 10 for two reasons:
- The block is dense: 6px gaps between the H1, price, ladder and delivery line, and five rupee figures plus a strike in 140px (fold_facts_zoom.png). The budget forces this; it is not a fault the builder can remove.
- The caption 'Mix any pieces, no code · the bracelet's price' is serviceable rather than graceful.

Seven real slides in a good arc (gallery_r4.jpg): worn, macro, plaster, the deep-blue velvet (the jeweller's-box contrast Indian shoppers read as fine jewellery), Riya, the ruler and the box. Slide 5 now names Riya once (the tag), and its plate says only 'Play'. The viewer shows the 896x1200 original with the lips-and-hand pose (viewer.png). That is the most editorial frame on the page, and it is right that it lives there rather than in a 309px hero.

Held under 9 by four things:
- riya-540 (0.75x) and velvet-640 (0.89x) are upscaled at DPR 2;
- slide 5 still carries three plates;
- the ruler slide is slight beside the photographs;
- Up close repeats slide 2's frame.

Type is a system:
- Cormorant 27/24/20/18/15 at weight 500 with lining figures;
- Jost 15/13/12/11;
- 24 text styles in the census (probe.json), with no half pixels and an 11px floor;
- tracked caps only on buttons, fold labels, dt labels, the bag kicker and the footer tagline.

Small faults:
- Four tracking values (.03, .04, .12, .14em) where two would do.
- In the bag, 'Total' rides at the top of the Cormorant 24 figure instead of on its baseline (drawer_1.png).
- At 320 the primary button's label has 2px between its letters and the button edge (bar320.js: content 14-170 in 12-172), so the main CTA looks squeezed.

Restraint is real:
- the colours in use are exactly ivory, ivory-deep, ink, ink at 72%, deep sage and two hairline alphas (probe.json), plus the white UPI discs;
- radius 0 except the bag's checkout;
- no badges, stars, timers or marquee;
- one ink primary;
- a 48px section rhythm;
- a deep-sage footer.
The reassurance list is now a quiet lead-plus-detail list instead of an icon-with-text block (scr_500.png). Next to the bench folds it sits with Mejuri.

What still looks heavy:
- The GPay, PhonePe and Paytm marks are the loudest pixels on the first screen. They are kept for C8, and brand rules forbid recolouring them.
- The set thumbnails sit on three grounds.
- The hole in the spec table.
- The bag's triple saving line.

Up from 8.4 (added_1.png, added_ring.png):
- both thumbnails are 48px, so the names align at x 85;
- the counter hides while the card is open;
- '✓ Added' is inert;
- the card spans 85-360, or 85-364 after the ring is added;
- the price, ladder and delivery line are never covered;
- the rung is underlined only once it applies.

Two idiom slips remain:
- The bracelet's ₹2,399 trails its name inline, while the set rows and the bag right-align every price.
- The ring's line breaks after the middle dot, 'PVD rhodium · / adjustable, US 5–9', leaving the dot at a line end. The bag's 'Wear it with' row repeats the same break (drawer_1.png).
